<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Talakad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Talakadu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Talakad is a town on the Kaveri river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mysore">Mysore</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, once the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ganga-dynasty">Western Ganga dynasty</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chola-empire">Cholas</a> took it around 1004, and its capture by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnuvardhana">Vishnuvardhana</a> in 1116 drove them from southern Karnataka; he took the title Talakadugonda, conqueror of Talakad. Many of its old temples now lie buried under drifting sand.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/talakad.jpg" alt="Talakad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dineshkannambadi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaidyeshvara_Temple_(1000_AD)_at_Talakad.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
